diff --git a/docs/runbooks/gateway-504.md b/docs/runbooks/gateway-504.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..56e2707
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/runbooks/gateway-504.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Runbook: gateway timeouts (504)
+
+Alert: `PaymentsGatewayTimeoutRate` fires when more than 2% of charge requests
+end in a gateway timeout over five minutes.
+
+## What the service does on its own
+
+A charge that times out is retried up to three times in total. Every attempt
+carries the same `Idempotency-Key`, so the gateway treats the retries as one
+charge and a customer is never billed twice.
+
+| Attempt | Wait before it |
+|---------|----------------|
+| 1       | none           |
+| 2       | 200 ms         |
+| 3       | 400 ms         |
+
+Only a 504 or a transport error is retried. Declined cards are not.
+
+## When the alert fires
+
+1. Check the gateway status page and the `#gateway-incidents` channel.
+2. Open the "Payments / Gateway" dashboard and look at "Attempts per charge".
+   A value near 3 means the gateway is failing consistently, not flaking.
+3. If the gateway is down, do nothing: charges fail fast with
+   `gateway_timeout` and merchants retry with the same key.
+4. If only our traffic is affected, check the egress proxy and DNS.
+
+## Tuning
+
+| Variable                 | Default | Effect                              |
+|--------------------------|---------|-------------------------------------|
+| `GATEWAY_RETRY_ATTEMPTS` | 3       | Total tries per charge              |
+| `GATEWAY_RETRY_DELAY`    | 200ms   | Wait before the second try          |
+| `GATEWAY_TIMEOUT`        | 10s     | Budget for all attempts of a charge |
+
+Do not raise the attempts above 5 without talking to the gateway team: during
+an outage every extra attempt multiplies the load they have to shed.
